  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Kay and Associates obligated $216M in FY2026 to date, across 34 awards with an average award size of $6.3M. Kay and Associates obligations are up 20.5% year over year. Kay and Associates received $179M in FY25 and $216M in FY26, after obligations of $117M in FY24, $137M in FY23, $111M in FY22, and $130M in FY21. The Department of Defense is Kay and Associates' primary buyer, obligating $216M so far in FY2026 to date, while the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $13.9K. Other Support Activities for Air Transportation is the largest market for Kay and Associates at $127M, followed by Aircraft Manufacturing at $88.3M and Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $13.9K. All figures are contract obligations except award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, which are total contract values, and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Kay and Associates' federal business trended recently?",
        "body": "Kay and Associates obligations rose to $216M in FY26, up 20.5% year over year. Kay and Associates obligations were $179M in FY25 and ranged from $111M to $137M in FY22–FY23, and $117M in FY24. The current-year total is partial, reflecting fiscal year to date activity."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who buys from Kay and Associates and in which markets?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the top buyer, obligating $216M in FY2026 to date. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $13.9K. Other Support Activities for Air Transportation is the top market at $127M, followed by Aircraft Manufacturing at $88.3M and Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $13.9K."
      }
    ]
